# DEMO 1: Code review with a correction loop
#
# reviewer reads the code -> finds bugs -> coder fixes them AND COMPILES
# -> reviewer checks again -> APPROVED -> done.
#
# ABOUT CONDITIONAL EDGES:
# reviewer must write NEEDS_FIX or APPROVED. If it forgets (happens with long
# responses), no conditional edge matches.
#
# The fallback goes to END, not to coder. Why: if we sent it to coder, and the
# reviewer forgot the marker every time, we would loop forever burning money.
# Better to stop and let the user see in the log what happened.
#
# Run:
#   ./pixelgo flow run demo demo/01-code-review.flow "Check src/calc.c"

entry reviewer

node reviewer
node coder

# normal decision (conditionals take priority over the fallback)
edge reviewer -> coder    when NEEDS_FIX
edge reviewer -> END      when APPROVED

# fallback: if the model gave no verdict, we stop (no looping)
edge reviewer -> END

# after a fix, reviewer checks again
edge coder -> reviewer
